		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="section__head">
				<p class="eyebrow">Conveyancing Services</p>
				<h2>Comprehensive Assistance for Selling a Property in NSW</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="conveyancing-intro">
        	<p class="conveyancing-intro__lead">    
				<p>We offer comprehensive conveyancing assistance for various types of conveyancing transactions in NSW.</p>
                <br>
                <p>Selling your property in NSW, be it your family home or an investment property, it is indeed a significant step that you are taking.<br><br>
                   It is a significant as it is something that you probably do not do regularly and something that you most likely be unaccustomed to doing. 
                   Selling a property in NSW can be an exciting time for you. Selling a property will also involve a number of challenges and time-consuming 
                   tasks. Some of these tasks may include: preparing your property for the market, engaging a Real Estate Agent, and making decisions about 
                   your next investment or place of residence. It's no wonder that selling real estate is widely considered one of the most stressful experiences
                   one can experience during your life.</p>
                   <p>
                   &nbsp;
                   </p>
			</div>
            
			<div class="instruments">
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">01</span>
					<h3>Residential Property Sales</h3>
					<p>Torrens Title houses and Strata Title units each call for a different set of prescribed documents before your agent can advertise. We prepare your contract with the planning certificate, title search and, for units, the strata information you are required to disclose, so your property reaches the market without delay.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/wills">Residential Property Sales</a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">02</span>
					<h3>Commercial Property Sales</h3>
					<p>Commercial sales bring GST and existing tenancies into the contract, and both change what you actually receive at settlement. We set out the GST treatment and your obligations to sitting tenants before a buyer makes an offer, including any going concern arrangement.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/power-of-attorney">Commercial Property Sales</a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">03</span>
					<h3>Retirement Village Sales</h3>
					<p>Exiting a retirement village works differently from a standard sale, yhis primarily is because the operator sits between you and the buyer. We review your village contract so you know what the deferred management fee and reinstatement costs will take out of your proceeds, then deal with the operator on your behalf.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Retirement Village Sales</a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">04</span>
					<h3>Vacant Land Sales</h3>
					<p>Vacant land contracts live or die on disclosure. We check your title for easements and restrictions and confirm what the planning certificate says about zoning, because a buyer who finds either problem after exchange may have grounds to rescind.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Vacant Land Sales</a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">05</span>
					<h3>Rural Land Sales</h3>
					<p>Rural sales carry items a suburban contract never touches, from water access licences to fencing agreements and stock arrangements. We identify what forms part of the sale and what stays with you, then draft the contract so nothing is left to interpretation on settlement day.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Rural Land Sales</a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">06</span>
					<h3>Put & Call Options</h3>
					<p>Put and call options let you lock in a buyer now and settle later, which suits vendors dealing with developers. We draft the option deed and set the timeframes carefully, so you understand what triggers each option and you are not left waiting on a buyer who never exercises.</p>
					<a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Put & Call Options</a>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>